<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imperial Airways</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1924">1924</a>–<a href="/years/1939">1939</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Imperial Airways was the British long-range airline formed in 1924 to link the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> by air. Its routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> needed landing grounds across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-east">Middle East</a>, and in 1932 it opened a rest house and airfield at Sharjah on the Gulf. It merged with British Airways Ltd in 1939 to form BOAC.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/imperial-airways.jpg" alt="Imperial Airways" width="320" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: San Diego Air &amp; Space Museum Archives · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:15_De_Havilland_D.H.91_Albatross_(15650662757).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
